From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: a windowed program's crash debugger shows no console (5973)

The debugger started for a crashed program (winedbg --auto, a console
program) got a console of its own when the program had none, and it came
up as a window: an empty "Debugger" terminal reading "WineDbg attached to
pid ..." behind the Program Error box (OneDrive's sync service on qa4).
Windows' crash reporter shows no console. It is started with
CREATE_NO_WINDOW then; the box is a window and still comes up. Gate
test/crashconsole-gate.sh (mutant DEBUGGER_CONSOLE).
---
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c
@@ -650,7 +650,16 @@
     startup.cb = sizeof(startup);
     startup.dwFlags = STARTF_USESHOWWINDOW;
     startup.wShowWindow = SW_SHOWNORMAL;
-    ret = CreateProcessW( NULL, cmdline, NULL, NULL, TRUE, CREATE_UNICODE_ENVIRONMENT, env, NULL, &startup, &info );
+    /* Stained Glass OS: a program with no console of its own crashed -- the
+     * debugger (winedbg, a console program) is given none to show. Its new
+     * console became a window of its own, an empty "Debugger" terminal behind
+     * the "Program Error" box (OneDrive's sync service, qa4); Windows' crash
+     * reporter shows no console. The box is a window and still comes up. */
+    ret = CreateProcessW( NULL, cmdline, NULL, NULL, TRUE, CREATE_UNICODE_ENVIRONMENT
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_DEBUGGER_CONSOLE
+                          | (NtCurrentTeb()->Peb->ProcessParameters->ConsoleHandle ? 0 : CREATE_NO_WINDOW)
+#endif
+                          , env, NULL, &startup, &info );
     FreeEnvironmentStringsW( env );
 
     if (ret)
